<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qashliq</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Isker, Kashlyk</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qashliq, also called Isker, was the capital of the Khanate of Sibir, on the right bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irtysh">Irtysh</a> near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tobolsk">Tobolsk</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>. The Taibugid rulers made it their seat around 1495, and in 1582 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a> of Yermak took it from Khan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuchum">Kuchum</a>. It was abandoned after the Russians founded Tobolsk nearby in 1587.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qashliq.jpg" alt="Qashliq" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gerardus Mercator · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CEM-15-Asia-Mercator-1595-Russia-2533.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
